      "content": "Wait, you mentioned goblins hoarding coins? That's a bit of a sudden jump from the forest analogy. How does the goblin analogy actually relate to the physics of the displacement current or the buildup of the electric field? I'm trying to see if there's a real scientific parallel here or if you're just using them as random characters.",
