      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, I'm following the \"dance\" part, but I'm still a bit confused. If the goblins are the charge carriers moving in the ballroom, where does the actual \"displacement current\" fit into this? Like, if the goblins are just dancing on the floor, how does that explain the current that exists even when no electrons are physically crossing the gap? Is there a way to explain that specific part of the physics using this same scenario?",
      "source": "evaluator"
